    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We first apply Proposition <a href="/tag/1FE805" data-tag="1FE805">5.3.5.11</a> to conclude that $\Ind _{\kappa }(f)$ is fully faithful. To prove that $\Ind _{\kappa }(f)$ is an equivalence, we must show that it generates $\Ind _{\kappa }(\calD )$ under $\kappa $-filtered colimits. Since $\Ind _{\kappa }(\calD )$ is generated under $\kappa $-filtered colimits by the essential image of the Yoneda embedding $j_{\calD }: \calD \rightarrow \Ind _{\kappa }(\calD )$. Let $D$ be an object of $\calD $. Then $D$ is a retract of $f(C)$ for some object $C \in \calC $. Then $j_{\calD }(D)$ is a retract of $(\Ind _{\kappa }(f) \circ j_{\calC })(C)$. Since $\Ind _{\kappa }(\calC )$ is idempotent complete (Corollary <a href="/tag/6BB67F" data-tag="6BB67F">4.4.5.16</a>), we conclude that $j_{\calD }(D)$ belongs to the essential image of $\Ind _{\kappa }(f)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
